{
  "id": 397542681,
  "iid": 20486,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "GSM A: Fix incorrect length for Direction of Altitude field in GAD parsing",
  "description": "### Summary\n\nThis PR fixes an issue in the `dissect_geographical_description()` function in `packet-gsm_a_common.c`, where the **Direction of Altitude (D)** bit was being extracted using an incorrect length (`1` byte) instead of the correct `2` bytes.\n\nThis applies to:\n- `ELLIPSOID_POINT_WITH_ALT`\n- `ELLIPSOID_POINT_WITH_ALT_AND_UNCERT_ELLIPSOID`\n\nThe D flag resides in the **most significant bit (bit 15)** of a **2-byte** field shared with the Altitude value. Parsing only 1 byte causes incorrect interpretation of the flag and results in display errors such as showing `D: 0` when the actual bit is set.\n\n---\n\n### Root Cause\n\nPrevious code:\n```c\nproto_tree_add_item(tree, hf_gsm_a_geo_loc_D, tvb, offset, 1, ENC_BIG_ENDIAN);\n```\n\nCorrected to:\n```c\nproto_tree_add_item(tree, hf_gsm_a_geo_loc_D, tvb, offset, 2, ENC_BIG_ENDIAN);\n```\nThis ensures proper access to the 16-bit field where:\n* Bit 15: Direction of Altitude\n* Bits 14–0: Altitude in meters\n\nReference\n* [3GPP TS 23.032 version 17.2.0 Release 17, section 7.3.5](https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/123000_123099/123032/17.02.00_60/ts_123032v170200p.pdf)\n* Current issue, where `Direction of Altitude` presented as `0`, the byte was `0x83e8`:<br/>\n![Screenshot_from_2025-07-09_09-21-39](/uploads/8e53357f8645933a10e66d004f6a2a63/Screenshot_from_2025-07-09_09-21-39.png)\n* Expected result:\n```sh\n        1... .... .... .... = D: Direction of Altitude: Altitude expresses depth (1)\n        .000 0011 1110 1000 = Altitude in meters: 1000\n```",
  "state": "merged",
